      "writtenOn": "2019-08-05T10:19:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The colon indicates that what follows is a name of a target that provides the files. The syntax is documented under filegroup:\n\n    filegroup contains a list of files that are referenced by other modules properties (such as \"srcs\") using the syntax \":\u003cname\u003e\". filegroup are also be used to export files across package boundaries.\n\nI believe this is a fairly self-evident notion (compare to Bazel\u0027s \":target-name\" syntax). I don\u0027t see it being documented at any other use sites.\n\nPlease note this is a cherry-pick change.",
      "parentUuid": "6e9ae0c1_c43cacfa",
